FAIL (fixable)

The Level 3 plan is complete, the creative record exists, and the four units are in test-then-code order. No change-detector steps to strike, and no test/code swap. File names match the dialect rules: `git-identity.bash` stays bash, `shims/gh.sh` is POSIX, tests stay in `tests/test-*.sh`, and the installer change stays out of the `-h` / cat-page loop. Those checks passed.

The shim read does not. Component analysis tells the shim to use `git config --get`. A read without `--local` walks system, global, then local, and returns a global `github.account` when the checkout never set one. Writes in unit 1 are fine: `git config --replace-all` inside a repository is local by default, and linked worktrees share that file. The bug is only the read. Requirement 5 says a missing pin leaves the environment unchanged. The planned suites set `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null`, so a cascade read goes green and the requirement still fails on a machine with a global key. Outside a repository the plan already execs unchanged, which is right; `git config --local` errors there, so the repo check has to stay first.

Fix: in unit 2, after the directory is confirmed to be a repository, read with `git config --local --get`. Exit 1 means unset. Add a behavior the current harness cannot hide: inside a repository, local key unset, `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL` pointed at a file that sets `github.account` to `example-login`, ambient `GH_TOKEN` preserved, and `auth token` not run. Add the same global key to the not-a-repository case so a cascade read fails that test too.

Advisory. Install-time real binary. The runtime PATH walk is the fragile part of unit 2, and step 4's "skip the directory of the running script" does not work when `$0` is bare `gh` (`dirname` is `.`). The challenges section already says to compare the candidate with the running script. A test that execs an absolute path goes green while a normal PATH invocation re-execs the shim. Alternative, if the cost is worth a redesign: resolve the real `gh` once in `install_gh_shim`, before the shim occupies `~/.local/bin/gh`. A foreign file is still moved to `~/.local/libexec/git-aliases/gh`. Otherwise, if that path is absent, symlink the first `gh` on a PATH that does not contain `~/.local/bin`. The shim then execs only the libexec path and exits non-zero when it is missing. Delete the PATH walk. On reinstall, refresh a symlink and do not replace a regular parked file. Uninstall moves a regular file back, and removes a symlink so the shell finds the next `gh`. Cost: a `gh` installed or moved after `make subcommands` stays invisible until the next install. That is the trade against deleting `$0`, spaces-in-PATH, and libexec-versus-PATH from the shim.

Advisory. `@gh-host` and the command host. Unit 2 passes `--hostname` only into `auth token`, then exports `GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN` or `GH_TOKEN` and does not set `GH_HOST`. Repo-scoped `gh` infers the host from the remote after SSH translation, so a remote that already names `ghe.example` works. A command that does not infer that host still targets `github.com` or ambient `GH_HOST` and will not read `GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN`. Exporting `GH_HOST` from `github.host` closes that gap. It also makes `gh` error when no remote matches, which is fail-closed, and it breaks a checkout whose remote is an SSH alias that does not translate to `github.host` (`cli/cli` `pkg/cmd/factory/remote_resolver.go`). The behavior list never covers a host ending in `.ghe.com`, which must stay on `GH_TOKEN`. The creative note still says an omitted host means github.com unless `GH_HOST` is already set; the plan should not be "fixed" back to always exporting `GH_TOKEN`.

Advisory. Empty `@gh-account`. The reader only calls `process_directive` when the line matches `@name` plus a value token, then strips one pair of quotes. `@gh-account ""` arrives empty and the planned non-zero exit works. A bare `@gh-account` falls through to `eval git config --replace-all`, and `git-identity.bash` has no `set -e`, so the use still exits 0. The empty-value test has to use the quoted form, or the reader has to change. That reader change is not in the unit.

Advisory. `git config --unset` exit 5. Keep the unset before the success `echo`. There is no `set -e`, so a trailing unset that returns 5 becomes `git identity use`'s exit status. No planned case unsets a key that was never set. `scripts/install-subcommands.sh` is `set -euo pipefail`: `mv` will not create `~/.local/libexec/git-aliases/`, and an unconditional restore of a missing parked file fails `make clean`. `test_uninstall_removes_help_pages` installs and uninstalls with no foreign `gh`, so it goes red until the restore is conditional. `memory-bank/productContext.md`'s constraint still says the only runtime dependencies are git and bash; the scheduled edit does not touch that sentence, and the pin needs the real `gh`.
